Note on third-party code: all files in this repository except economy.js and
letter-map/ are a JavaScript port of hadsh/nms_namegen
(https://github.com/hadsh/nms_namegen), itself a fork of Stuart Coyle's
original nms_namegen (https://github.com/stu-/nms_namegen), co-authored with
GoodGuysFree. hadsh's repository states this work is MIT-licensed. The MIT
license above applies to elegra1965's original code (economy.js, the port
itself as a JavaScript adaptation); it does not make elegra1965 the author of
the underlying reverse-engineered generation algorithms. Each ported file
additionally carries its own "Ported from hadsh/nms_namegen (MIT licensed)"
attribution comment with the upstream URL, per MIT's own requirement that the
original notice travel with the code. Credit for the underlying algorithms
belongs to Stuart Coyle (original author), GoodGuysFree (co-author of the
hadsh fork), and hadsh (fork maintainer).

Exception: the sellBuy() function in system.js (the real sell%/buy%
formula, found 2026-10-13) is elegra1965's own original work and was not
ported from hadsh/nms_namegen. Anyone using it should credit elegra1965 /
No Man's Sky Hub (https://nomansskyhub.app).

Note on game assets: No Man's Sky and all related game data are the property
of Hello Games. The probability tables in economy.js were decompiled from a
legitimately-owned install for research and interoperability purposes. This
module is a fan project and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed
by Hello Games.
